WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:05.330
Following the huge success of Bird Box, the
apocalypse has returned to Netflix, though

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:09.740
this time it's a swarm of prehistoric-style
creatures that threaten to wipe out humanity.

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:14.200
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm revealing behind-the-scenes

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:19.140
secrets about the monsters in The Silence,
explaining who the sinister cult really are,

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:21.609
and I'll talk about how the movie compares
to A Quiet Place.

00:00:21.609 --> 00:00:23.220
Plus I'll talk about how the movie compares
to A Quiet Place.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:25.051
Obviously, spoilers ahead, so take care if
you haven't seen the film yet.

00:00:25.051 --> 00:00:30.419
The Silence's pterodactyl-like monsters, the
Vesps, are unleashed when an archaeological

00:00:30.419 --> 00:00:34.770
expedition opens up an uncharted cave system
deep in the mountains.

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:39.110
The Vesps are an undiscovered species that
had been sealed underground and so although

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:43.760
they're blind, they've evolved an acute sense
of hearing so they hunt their prey by sound.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:48.120
The movie's producer said the filmmakers created
a mythology and back story for the monsters

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:52.680
where after they got stuck in the cave system,
the Vesps "adjusted to living life in darkness

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:54.390
with limited resources.

00:00:54.390 --> 00:00:59.030
They evolved and developed the ability to
shut down their system into a sort of stasis,

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:01.400
and they didn't need a lot of fuel to stay
alive."

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:06.159
After the Vesps escape into the world above,
they have access to a lot more food and are

00:01:06.159 --> 00:01:08.860
therefore able to reproduce much more quickly.

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:13.200
As Ally discovers when she and her father
are at the pharmacy, these creatures lay eggs

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:14.729
inside their victims.

00:01:14.729 --> 00:01:19.729
The Vesps' physiology and design is inspired
by reptiles, bats, and birds, and they are

00:01:19.729 --> 00:01:23.359
meant to be a naturalistic species that could
have evolved on Earth.

00:01:23.359 --> 00:01:27.149
Director John Leonetti explained that they
researched "species that have been found in

00:01:27.149 --> 00:01:31.619
caves over the years and used that to make
the Vesps' biology very realistic […]

00:01:31.619 --> 00:01:35.909
Their skin is translucent, they have wings
and they fly, but they also crawl and lay

00:01:35.909 --> 00:01:37.479
eggs like reptiles.

00:01:37.479 --> 00:01:42.139
A lot of scientific research went into the
design, the creation, and the computer animation

00:01:42.139 --> 00:01:46.789
of the creatures, right down to the detail
of every joint, every vessel, and every move

00:01:46.789 --> 00:01:47.789
they make."

00:01:47.789 --> 00:01:52.430
The filmmakers have also said the monsters
are definitely not aliens or creatures from

00:01:52.430 --> 00:01:57.509
outer space, and they're named after the Spanish
word for wasps, avispas, as they tend to swarm

00:01:57.509 --> 00:01:59.960
in large numbers, attacking their prey.

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:04.560
The Vesps' ability to evolve and reproduce
so quickly is their strength, and as we see

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:09.010
at the very end of the movie, even though
it's reported they don't like extreme cold,

00:02:09.010 --> 00:02:11.769
some of them are now making their way north
and surviving.

00:02:11.769 --> 00:02:17.430
Ally who made it to the Refuge, which is located
in a snowy, cold area, is now hunting down

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:19.769
Vesps which have invaded the territory.

00:02:19.769 --> 00:02:23.569
And what's most scary is that the Vesps have
been laying their eggs in the animals they've

00:02:23.569 --> 00:02:26.470
killed in the area, for example, this wolf.

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:30.909
It seems like a pretty grim apocalyptic ending,
but Ally suggests there is a possibility that

00:02:30.909 --> 00:02:35.599
humanity could survive this disaster and beat
the monsters that are slowly overtaking the

00:02:35.599 --> 00:02:36.599
world.

00:02:36.599 --> 00:02:38.439
"So, will the rest of humanity evolve?

00:02:38.439 --> 00:02:43.980
Will we adapt to this new world of silence
and remember what it is that separates us

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:44.980
from them?

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:45.980
Maybe.

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:49.049
I guess it's just a question of which of the
two species does it first."

00:02:49.049 --> 00:02:53.560
According to Ally, she herself is proof it's
possible for humans to evolve.

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:57.190
After an accident where she lost her hearing,
she explains that her father was surprised

00:02:57.190 --> 00:02:59.219
that she adapted so quickly.

00:02:59.219 --> 00:03:03.110
And as a result of that, Ally and her family
learned to communicate with sign language,

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:07.159
which meant they seemed more equipped to live
in a world where silence means safety and

00:03:07.159 --> 00:03:09.700
noise leads to danger, even death.

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:13.140
The final scene, which has a touch of The
Hunger Games about it, shows that Ally has

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:17.250
figured out one way to kill the creatures
is using a bow and arrow, which is obviously

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:19.209
much quieter than a gun.

00:03:19.209 --> 00:03:23.810
That's also why earlier in the movie Hugh
fashioned a wooden spear as a weapon for Jude

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:24.860
to use.

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:29.250
At the end of the day, though, given how rapidly
the creatures seem to multiply laying so many

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:33.950
eggs, surviving families would really need
a larger scale solution such as the wood chipper

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:37.000
Ally's father used earlier in the film.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:41.250
As well as the Vesps, The Silence also has
a group of human antagonists who the family

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:42.469
have to deal with.

00:03:42.469 --> 00:03:46.170
Following Ally and her father's trip to the
pharmacy, they have their first encounter

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:49.750
with the creepy Reverend who tries to get
them to join his flock.

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:54.249
The Reverend leads a group or cult called
The Hushed who've cut out their own tongues

00:03:54.249 --> 00:03:57.900
and later they turn up at the place where
Ally and her family are staying to pressure

00:03:57.900 --> 00:03:59.989
them again to join their cult.

00:03:59.989 --> 00:04:04.670
This time it's even more creepy though because
the Reverend reveals he's after Ally in particular

00:04:04.670 --> 00:04:06.450
because she's fertile.

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:10.590
It's never stated explicitly, but it seems
the cult may be collecting young women to

00:04:10.590 --> 00:04:16.019
use them to breed and swell their own numbers
and repopulate the earth after the Apocalypse.

00:04:16.019 --> 00:04:20.669
By the way, this is a change from the original
book by Tim Lebbon where the cult wanted Ally

00:04:20.669 --> 00:04:23.770
so they could learn to sign and communicate
silently.

00:04:23.770 --> 00:04:27.889
The Hushed also seem to be part of a broader
religious reaction to the unleashing of this

00:04:27.889 --> 00:04:29.360
apocalyptic world.

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:34.580
At one point in the movie when Ally is on
her tablet, we see headlines that say religious

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:38.520
extremists have been breeding the creatures
to hasten the end of the world or what they

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:40.490
see as Judgement Day.

00:04:40.490 --> 00:04:44.970
They've also been burning atheists alive and
one preacher is reported as saying humanity

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:47.210
is the plague and Vesps are the cure.

00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:51.710
In fact, when Ally calls her boyfriend Rob,
he's coughing and looks like he's holed up

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:53.949
somewhere trying to keep safe.

00:04:53.949 --> 00:04:57.789
Rob tells Ally his parents are dead and I
wonder if that's because they've been attacked

00:04:57.789 --> 00:04:59.770
by religious fanatics?

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:04.150
The Silence also plays on the idea of this
religious cult as terrorists when they send

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:08.979
a young girl into the house wearing a suicide
vest made up of cell phones ready to go off.

00:05:08.979 --> 00:05:14.639
OK, so, you've no doubt heard a lot of people
saying this movie's a rip-off of A Quiet Place.

00:05:14.639 --> 00:05:19.190
Before I explain why A Quiet Place is definitely
a much better film, it's worth noting that

00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:23.250
The Silence was actually adapted from a book
written by Tim Lebbon which was published

00:05:23.250 --> 00:05:27.939
before A Quiet Place came out, so it's not
a rip-off even if the premise is similar.

00:05:27.939 --> 00:05:32.210
The way A Quiet Place executed the idea though
is much better.

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:37.110
It has a much tighter story focussing on just
one family with barely any other characters

00:05:37.110 --> 00:05:41.849
or speaking in the movie and so the tension
in that film is really dialled up to the max

00:05:41.849 --> 00:05:46.580
as the family avoids making even a tiny noise
for fear of attracting the monsters stalking

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:47.580
the land.

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:50.350
The Silence, by contrast, is all over the
place.

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:54.639
The family mostly talks even when they're
signing and the story moves way too quickly

00:05:54.639 --> 00:05:59.160
taking the family from the suburbs, to the
countryside and then on to the Refuge in less

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:03.830
than 90 minutes, with a side plot of religious
extremism along the way.

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:09.669
On top of that, each death in A Quiet Place
has much more impact than those in The Silence.

00:06:09.669 --> 00:06:13.580
That's because The Silence's characters are
underdeveloped so you don't care as much about

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:18.500
what happens to them, and although the religious
cult side story is potentially interesting,

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:21.169
it comes late in the film and feels rushed
through.

00:06:21.169 --> 00:06:25.509
Also, many points which come up in the film
are left hanging, for example, the fact that

00:06:25.509 --> 00:06:29.949
the electric grid and internet seems to be
randomly working and then sometimes not.

00:06:29.949 --> 00:06:32.510
Is it because the creatures have been taking
down power lines?

00:06:32.510 --> 00:06:37.389
I mean we see them massing on power lines,
or is it something else?

00:06:37.389 --> 00:06:42.130
Like both A Quiet Place and Bird Box showed,
the idea of a creature preying on one of your

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:47.210
senses can set up a very interesting horror
movie and The Silence, like those two other

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:52.810
films, also has a good cast including Kiernan
Shipka, Stanley Tucci and Miranda Otto.

00:06:52.810 --> 00:06:56.789
Unfortunately, they can only really do their
best with the material they're given which

00:06:56.789 --> 00:07:00.270
doesn't live up to either A Quiet Place or
Bird Box.

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:04.699
A Quiet Place also did a great job casting
a talented deaf actress as one of the main

00:07:04.699 --> 00:07:08.850
characters, whereas some in the deaf community
have criticised The Silence for using a hearing

00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:13.379
actress in the role of Ally as well as for
an inconsistent and sometimes unrealistic

00:07:13.379 --> 00:07:18.169
approach to both signing and lip reading and
the fact that there's much more to being deaf

00:07:18.169 --> 00:07:20.389
than simply sign language.

00:07:20.389 --> 00:07:24.599
On the positive side, The Silence does a decent
job with the design and look of the Vesps

00:07:24.599 --> 00:07:26.729
and they do work quite effectively.

